# Wattleflow documentation — publication scope.
#
# Purpose of the public edition: presenting the project (marketing). Published are the
# doctrinal layer and the requirement registers (HLRQ, FRQ, NFRQ) with the styles their
# diagrams include. Not published: analyses (*-ANL.md, 06-ANALYSIS), method documents
# (05-METHODS), alignment records (07-CHANGES), the policy cascade that steers the agent
# (CLAUDE.md, POLICY.md, STANDARDS.md, DOCUMENTATION.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, DECISIONS.md,
# CONFORMANCE.md), tools, generated glossary, per-distribution trees and dockers.
#
# Rule: everything is ignored unless listed below. A document enters publication by adding
# its own `!` line; links from published texts to unlisted files are written as plain code
# spans, never as links (tools/links.py checks the tree).

# --- Ignore everything ----------------------------------------------------
/*

# --- Repository essentials -------------------------------------------------
!/.gitignore
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/images/
/images/*
!/images/wattleflow.png
!/images/FRQ-BBD-1.png
!/images/FRQ-BBD-class-diagram.png
!/images/FRQ-BBD-sequence-diagram.png
!/images/FRQ-BBD-state-machine-diagram.png
!/images/FRQ-DRV-class-diagram.png
!/images/NFRQ-000-INDEX.png
!/images/NFRQ-APX-01.png

# --- Doctrinal layer and vocabulary ---------------------------------------
!/PHILOSOPHY.md
!/DOCTRINE.md
!/METHODOLOGY.md
!/POSTULATE.md
!/LITERATURE.md
!/DICTIONARY.md
!/dictionary.yaml

# --- Requirement registers -------------------------------------------------
!/requirements/
/requirements/*

!/requirements/01-HLRQ/
!/requirements/02-FRQ/
!/requirements/03-NFRQ/
!/requirements/DIAGRAMS.md

# Analyses stay in the working tree only.
*-ANL.md

# PlantUML and CSS styles included by every inline diagram and rendered page.
!/requirements/styles/

# --- Never ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.*
!.gitignore
